Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: ranking is unstable and several models have correlated errors; testing inverse-error weighting may give a better weighted blend.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: The series has strong seasonality and unstable ranking; a trimmed mean could reduce influence of outlier models.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: The series has unstable rankings and strong seasonality; a DBA blend may capture dominant patterns while down‑weighting outliers.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: test a per‑model weight that down‑weights high‑error models via softmax, a different weighting family from inverse_error.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"softmax_neg_error"}

Thought: The series has unstable rankings and correlated errors; a forward selection weight might capture complementary models better than static inverse or softmax weights.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"forward"}

Thought: test a weighting that adapts to error trends across windows, since ranking is unstable and some models improve while others degrade (error_trend).  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"error_trend"}

Thought: The series has strong seasonality and unstable ranking; a robust median blend may reduce influence of extreme models while still capturing diverse patterns.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: The series shows high outliers and unstable ranking; a per‑horizon best‑model weighting may capture changing dominance across horizons.  
Action: weights_topk_per_horizon  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","k":5,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: test a per‑horizon weighted blend with top‑k mean (w6) to capture horizon‑varying strengths in this seasonal series.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w6"}

Thought: Try a softmax‑negative‑error weighted blend to see if a different weighting family beats the current DBA leader.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"softmax_neg_error"}

Thought: The series has unstable rankings and strong seasonality; a per‑horizon best‑model weighting could capture horizon‑specific strengths.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"best_per_horizon"}

Thought: Use a metric‑ranked subset (top‑k) to reduce variance and test inverse‑error weighting on that set, addressing unstable ranking and high outlier pct.  
Action: select_top_k  
Action Input: {"k":7,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: test a weighted blend on the top‑ranked pool (trend & seasonality strong, ranking unstable) using inverse_error to see if a simpler weight can beat DBA.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool4","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: The series shows strong seasonality and unstable rankings; per‑horizon weighting may capture horizon‑varying strengths across the 8‑week horizon.

Action: weights_topk_per_horizon

